OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,$A(E)
OL,3,GNEWSAKey takeaways from BBC interview
OL,4,Aas Earl Spencer defends claims about
OL,5,AKing
OL,6,
OL,7,FAmong claims made in Swan Song about
OL,8,Fthe King, who was then the Prince of
OL,9,FWales, was that he said "we'll forget
OL,10,Fher soon enough" during an argument
OL,11,Fover whether Princes William and Harry
OL,12,Fshould walk in Diana's funeral
OL,13,Fprocession.
OL,15,FIn a strongly worded response,
OL,16,FBuckingham Palace said the King was
OL,17,F"mindful that the pain of fraternal
OL,18,Fgrief can cloud reason, affect
OL,19,Fjudgement and colour memory in ways
OL,20,Fothers do not recognise, even many
OL,21,Fyears after such a loss".
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
